<p class="kicker">Open debate</p>
<h1>Challenge our ideas</h1>
<p class="lede">A charter that can't survive criticism can't credibly call itself free.</p>
<p>We want objections before we want endorsements. Good-faith criticism that changes the standard gets credited in the change history.</p>

<h2>Questions we can't yet answer</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Is this substantively new, or open source with pirate branding?</li>
  <li>Can a public-domain ideal coexist with contribution attribution, trademark and patent rights?</li>
  <li>What does genuine data ownership mean for collaborative, organizational or publicly replicated records?</li>
  <li>Where does full process disclosure end to protect secrets, privacy, security and third-party rights?</li>
  <li>Can labor, taxes, reserves and risk be honestly represented in cost-based pricing?</li>
  <li>Who audits the auditors, conformance badges and costs?</li>
  <li>Could a project comply technically while using coercive or abusive hosted-service terms?</li>
  <li>Can smaller maintainers participate without onerous documentation overhead?</li>
  <li>What should survive a protocol or cloud provider disappearing?</li>
  <li>Would a competing fork have the right to continue the movement's symbols and specification?</li>
</ol>
<p>These are quoted from <a href="/governance/">the governance document</a>. The <a href="{% sourceLink "DECISIONS-AND-QUESTIONS.md" %}">decision register</a> lists twelve more open design decisions.</p>

<h2>Where to argue</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="{{ repoUrl }}/issues/new?template=what-would-make-this-fail.md">What Would Make This Fail?</a> — adversarial criticism and failure modes.</li>
  <li><a href="{{ repoUrl }}/issues/new?template=charter-rfc.md">Charter RFC</a> — propose or contest a specific requirement.</li>
  <li><a href="{{ repoUrl }}/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a>: open for general debate. The charter-specific categories and seed RFCs proposed in <a href="{% sourceLink "launch/RFC-SEEDS.md" %}"><code>launch/RFC-SEEDS.md</code></a> are <span class="badge pending">not yet posted</span>.</li>
</ul>
<p>You can read everything here without an account. Posting currently needs a GitHub account, and we count that as a dependency to remove.</p>
<p>No harassment, no private data, no fabricated evidence.</p>

<h2 id="rfcs">RFCs and open debates</h2>
<p>Every entry is a draft in the repository; none has been posted to Discussions yet (<a href="{{ repoUrl }}/issues/8">issue #8</a>). Each RFC states its own strongest objection. Agents can read these with <code>list_debates</code> and <code>get_debate</code>; see <a href="/agents/">For AI agents</a>.</p>
